@startuml
' Figure 32.4  Non-human identity lifecycle
' Reading order: left to right from requested to retired. Every
' identity has an owner before it is issued, a date it must be
' rotated or reviewed by, and a way out; a run token skips rotation
' and simply expires.
!include plantuml-theme.puml
hide empty description
[*] --> Requested
Requested --> Issued : Owner named,\nscopes reviewed
Issued --> Active : First use
Active --> Active : Rotated\nby its date
Active --> Suspended : Finding opened
Suspended --> Active : Finding closed
Active --> Revoked : Unused, or\nowner gone
Suspended --> Revoked : Not closed\nby its date
Issued --> Expired : Run token,\n15 minutes
Active --> Expired : Run token,\n15 minutes
Revoked --> [*]
Expired --> [*]
@enduml
